  "solution": "Factor out the common term \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n4x^3+5x^2-8x=0\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx(4x^2+5x-8)=0\n\\]\n\nSo one root is \\(x=0\\). The sum of all roots of a cubic can be found using Vieta’s formula:\n\nFor \\(ax^3+bx^2+cx+d=0\\), the sum of the roots is\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{b}{a}\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(a=4\\), \\(b=5\\), so\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum}=\\frac{-5}{4}=-1.25\n\\]\n\nThe answer is -1.25.",
